-## 10. Appendix
+## 10. Rate Limiting Configuration
 
-### 10.1 Student Profile JSON Schema `student_v1.schema.json`
+The standalone API gateway reads IP rate-limiting settings from
+`config/gateway.conf`. Edit these fields in `G_GATEWAY_CONF` and rebuild the
+gateway:
+
+```c
+.rate_limit_enabled              = true,
+.rate_limit_requests             = 100,
+.rate_limit_window_seconds       = 60,
+.rate_limit_v1                   = RL(60, 60),
+.rate_limit_v2                   = RL(500, 60)
+```
+
+| Key | Type | Description |
+|-----|------|-------------|
+| `rate_limit_enabled` | `true` / `false` | Enables or disables gateway-wide IP rate limiting. |
+| `rate_limit_requests` | integer | Default maximum requests allowed from one client IP during a window when no version-specific limit exists. |
+| `rate_limit_window_seconds` | integer | Default window size, in seconds, before the per-IP request count resets. |
+| `rate_limit_v1` | `RL(requests, seconds)` | Version-specific limit for public `v1` API clients. |
+| `rate_limit_v2` | `RL(requests, seconds)` | Version-specific limit for premium partner `v2` API clients. |
+
+Version-specific limits override the default global values. Unknown or unversioned
+requests fall back to `rate_limit_requests` and `rate_limit_window_seconds`.
+
+When enabled, requests over the configured limit receive **429 Too Many
+Requests** with a JSON error response.
+
